GCC 13.3's libstdc++ std::to_array() default-constructs the array and
assigns each element. A struct with const members has neither, so
SkFontHost_FreeType.cpp does not compile with x86_64-unknown-haiku-gcc
13.3.0. The table is static constexpr, so it stays constant without the
const on its members. Upstream status: not reported. Applies to Skia
chrome/m158 707e33875f.

--- a/src/ports/SkFontHost_FreeType.cpp
+++ b/src/ports/SkFontHost_FreeType.cpp
@@ -2262,8 +2262,8 @@
         struct CommonWeights {
             // Must remain the first member: the lookup below indexes with a
             // sizeof(CommonWeights) stride starting at &commonWeights[0].name.
-            char const * const name;
-            int const weight;
+            char const * name;
+            int weight;
         };
         // SkStrLCSearch binary searches this table, so the names must be lower-case and sorted.
         // There are probably more common names, but these are known to exist.
